ing the brand-new sea  lion exhibit our attendance has  increased over fourteen percent from  last year to this year those type of  expansions would not have been possible  under just city management because the  zoo is never going to be able to compete  with streets and safety about 75% of the  accredited urban zoos and aquariums in  this country are run through  public-private partnerships and that's  something many citizens probably don't  even notice is they think that their  city is the one that's running the zoo  when in fact the city may technically  own that asset but it's the private  sector through nonprofit arrangements  that are actually operating those  amenities and actually investing more  then the cities would be able to do  themselves under constrained budgets  you
 

